<main class="legal-page"><header class="legal-hero legal-terms-hero"><p>TRAVELTOURISM TERMS</p><h1>Clear expectations<br><em>for every journey.</em></h1><div><span>Effective 5 September 2026</span><span>Website, enquiries and booking requests</span></div></header>
<div class="legal-layout"><aside><p>ON THIS PAGE</p><nav><a href="#agreement">01 · Agreement</a><a href="#requests">02 · Booking requests</a><a href="#prices">03 · Prices &amp; payment</a><a href="#changes">04 · Changes &amp; cancellation</a><a href="#traveller">05 · Traveller duties</a><a href="#suppliers">06 · Suppliers &amp; liability</a><a href="#contact">07 · Contact</a></nav><div><strong>Before you book</strong><p>Website packages are invitations to enquire. A request becomes confirmed only after availability, price and terms are accepted.</p></div></aside>
<article><section class="legal-opening"><p>These Terms &amp; Conditions govern your use of the TravelTourism website and any enquiry or booking request submitted through it. Please read them before requesting a service.</p><p>Package-specific written terms supplied during confirmation, including payment and cancellation terms, form part of your agreement and take priority where they clearly differ from general website information.</p></section>
<section id="agreement"><span>01</span><h2>Using this website</h2><p>You must use the website lawfully and provide information that is accurate to the best of your knowledge. You may browse packages for personal travel planning. You may not interfere with website operation, attempt unauthorised access, submit malicious material, misuse another person’s identity, scrape content at unreasonable scale, or reproduce site content for commercial use without permission.</p><p>You must be at least 18 years old and legally able to enter an agreement to make a booking. If you arrange travel for others, you confirm that you are authorised to provide their information and accept relevant terms on their behalf.</p></section>
<section id="requests"><span>02</span><h2>Enquiries and booking requests</h2><p>Submitting a contact form or booking request does not itself create a confirmed reservation. It asks us to review the selected package, dates, travellers and preferences. A booking is confirmed only after we communicate availability and final price, you accept the applicable package and supplier terms, and any required deposit or payment is received and acknowledged.</p><p>Availability can change before confirmation. We may decline or ask you to revise a request when information is incomplete, a service is unavailable, pricing has changed, or the request cannot reasonably be fulfilled.</p></section>
<section id="prices"><span>03</span><h2>Prices, inclusions and payment</h2><p>Displayed prices are generally starting prices per person unless a page states otherwise. The final price may vary with dates, group size, room type, transport, taxes, permits, foreign exchange, supplier availability and requested changes. Inclusions and exclusions shown on the package page should be reviewed before confirmation.</p><p>We will communicate the accepted payment method, deposit, balance deadline and any supplier-specific conditions before confirmation. Do not send payment to an account or person that has not been verified through our official communication.</p></section>
<section id="changes"><span>04</span><h2>Changes, cancellations and refunds</h2><p>Requests to change or cancel a booking should be made promptly through our contact details. Charges and refund eligibility depend on the confirmed package terms, timing of the request, non-refundable components, supplier rules and costs already incurred. Air, rail, visa, permit, hotel and activity components may each have separate conditions.</p><p>If a confirmed service must be changed because a supplier becomes unavailable, safety requires it, or an event beyond reasonable control affects delivery, we may propose a reasonable alternative, reschedule, credit or refund according to the confirmed terms and amounts recoverable from suppliers.</p></section>
<section id="traveller"><span>05</span><h2>Traveller responsibilities</h2><ul><li>Check names, dates, itinerary, inclusions, exclusions and contact details before confirmation.</li><li>Hold valid passports, visas, permits, identification, insurance and health documentation required for the journey.</li><li>Assess whether the itinerary and activities suit each traveller’s health, mobility and experience.</li><li>Follow local law, supplier instructions, check-in times, safety directions and respectful conduct standards.</li><li>Tell us about relevant dietary, accessibility or medical needs early enough for us to ask suppliers what can be accommodated.</li></ul><p>Travel insurance appropriate to the destination, activities, medical needs and cancellation risk is strongly recommended.</p></section>
<section id="suppliers"><span>06</span><h2>Third-party suppliers and website information</h2><p>Hotels, carriers, guides, activity operators and other suppliers may provide parts of a journey under their own terms. We are not responsible for a supplier’s independent acts beyond the extent required by applicable law, though we will make reasonable efforts to assist when a service issue is reported.</p><p>Descriptions, maps, photographs, travel times and itineraries are provided to help planning and may be illustrative. Routes, operating hours, weather, local conditions and attractions can change. Website availability does not guarantee that every displayed element will be available for the requested date.</p></section>
<section><span>07</span><h2>Intellectual property, liability and disputes</h2><p>The website design, writing, branding and original media belong to TravelTourism or their respective licensors and are protected by applicable law. To the extent permitted by law, TravelTourism is not liable for indirect or consequential loss arising from website use, events outside reasonable control, or a traveller’s failure to meet stated responsibilities. Nothing in these terms excludes rights or liability that cannot lawfully be excluded.</p><p>These terms are governed by the laws of India. The parties should first try to resolve a concern in good faith through written communication. Subject to applicable consumer rights and mandatory law, courts with jurisdiction in Mumbai, Maharashtra will have jurisdiction over unresolved disputes.</p></section>
